From fb5f35e05298f3405b71284df5cc3f5e18be23f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 09:02:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 246/246] www: i18n quote-safety - dict tokens must not sit in
 single-quoted JS strings

Translations with apostrophes (FR/UK/TR/... - dicts escape \" but never ')
broke the JS of any page embedding a <#token#> in a '...' literal, killing
the UI for those languages only (v1.8.6a EU field reports: FR+UK broke
reaper_shell/Main_ReaperDash, FR+TR broke Reaper_Traffic).

Convert all 333 single-quoted token literals in reaper-owned www files to
template literals (safe in JS blocks and inside dq HTML attrs) or dq where
the quote is an HTML attribute delimiter. Validated: every inline script
block of these pages rendered in all 25 languages parses clean (node);
pre-fix image reproduces exactly the 5 known failures, post-fix zero.

Gate: reaper_verify.sh check 16 (reaper_langcheck.py) now fails the build
if any reaper www file embeds a token in a quote-context breakable by any
language. Shared fix - cherry-pick to be96u-only + all sibling branches.
